# This file holds no fingerprints on purpose.
#
# A gitleaks fingerprint for a directory scan names a path, a rule and a line. It
# does not name the matched value, so a real credential pasted on a pinned line
# would inherit the exception, and any edit above the line breaks the pin. The old
# pins were re-made after almost every change to a test file, and six of them had
# stopped matching anything without CI noticing.
#
# Reviewed false positives now live in .gitleaks.toml as [[allowlists]] entries
# bound to the exact matched value and, for fixtures, to one file. Add a new
# fixture there, not here. scripts/release/test_gitleaks_config.py fails if this
# file gains a fingerprint, and fails on an allowlist entry that matches nothing.
